Subject: Skip the @@hasInstance lookup for a plain function in instanceof

What this does
  Adds a fast path at the top of JS_IsInstanceOf for a plain function whose
  [[Prototype]] is Function.prototype and which has no own @@hasInstance.

Why we need it
  JS_IsInstanceOf always performs Get(obj, @@hasInstance), calls the resulting C
  function and converts its result to boolean, on every instanceof. For a plain
  bytecode or C function that lookup can only resolve to the built-in
  js_function_hasInstance, whose entire body is a call to
  JS_OrdinaryIsInstanceOf -- so the property lookup, the C-function dispatch and
  the ToBool round trip all happen for nothing.

What it adds
  A class test, a prototype test and an own-property test, then a direct call to
  JS_OrdinaryIsInstanceOf. No invalidation bit is needed because
  Function.prototype[@@hasInstance] is installed non-writable and
  non-configurable, so the property the lookup would find cannot change for the
  life of the realm. A function carrying its own @@hasInstance, a bound
  function, a Proxy, a class with a static @@hasInstance and every non-callable
  right-hand side keep the existing lookup. No opcode is added or retired and
  BC_VERSION is unchanged, so the built-in blobs are not regenerated.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -10407,6 +10407,19 @@
 
     if (!JS_IsObject(obj))
         goto fail;
+    /* A plain function whose [[Prototype]] is Function.prototype and which has
+       no own @@hasInstance can only resolve @@hasInstance to the builtin
+       js_function_hasInstance, whose whole body is a call to
+       JS_OrdinaryIsInstanceOf. Function.prototype[@@hasInstance] is installed
+       non-writable and non-configurable, so no invalidation is needed. */
+    {
+        JSObject *p = JS_VALUE_GET_OBJ(obj);
+        if ((p->class_id == JS_CLASS_BYTECODE_FUNCTION ||
+             p->class_id == JS_CLASS_C_FUNCTION) &&
+            p->shape->proto == JS_VALUE_GET_OBJ(ctx->function_proto) &&
+            !find_own_property1(p, JS_ATOM_Symbol_hasInstance))
+            return JS_OrdinaryIsInstanceOf(ctx, val, obj);
+    }
     method = JS_GetProperty(ctx, obj, JS_ATOM_Symbol_hasInstance);
     if (JS_IsException(method))
         return -1;
